## Running Individual Steps Manually

### Single write benchmark (one table type)

```bash
./02_write_benchmark.sh COPY_ON_WRITE logical
./02_write_benchmark.sh MERGE_ON_READ logical
./02_write_benchmark.sh COPY_ON_WRITE no_logical
./02_write_benchmark.sh MERGE_ON_READ no_logical
```

### Single read benchmark (one table, one JAR)

```bash
JARS=/home/hadoop/hudi-jars
S3=s3://performance-benchmark-datasets-us-west-2/hudi-bench/pavijars

# Read COW logical with 0.15.0
/home/hadoop/spark-3.5.0-bin-hadoop3/bin/spark-submit \
    --conf spark.driver.memory=8g \
    --conf spark.executor.memory=6g \
    --conf spark.executor.cores=3 \
    --conf spark.dynamicAllocation.enabled=true \
    --jars $JARS/hudi-spark3.5-bundle_2.12-0.15.0.jar \
    ./03_read_benchmark.py \
    --table-path   $S3/data/hudi_cow_logical \
    --label        cow_logical_0.15.0 \
    --schema-type  logical

# Read COW logical with 0.16.0-SNAPSHOT
/home/hadoop/spark-3.5.0-bin-hadoop3/bin/spark-submit \
    --conf spark.driver.memory=8g \
    --conf spark.executor.memory=6g \
    --conf spark.executor.cores=3 \
    --conf spark.dynamicAllocation.enabled=true \
    --jars $JARS/hudi-spark3.5-bundle_2.12-0.16.0-SNAPSHOT.jar \
    ./03_read_benchmark.py \
    --table-path   $S3/data/hudi_cow_logical \
    --label        cow_logical_0.16.0-SNAPSHOT \
    --schema-type  logical
```

