## Troubleshooting

### Out of memory during write
Increase executor memory in `02_write_benchmark.sh`:
```bash
--conf "spark.executor.memory=10g"
```

### HoodieStreamer picks up no new records on write 2/3/4
Verify the staging batch was actually copied into the source root:
```bash
aws s3 ls s3://.../data/wide_500cols_10000parts/ --recursive | grep batch_
```

### Schema mismatch error on write 3 (after JAR upgrade)
This is expected if the schema fix changes the Avro type of timestamp columns
(ts-micros → ts-millis). The 0.16.0-SNAPSHOT JAR handles this automatically.
Check the Hudi commit metadata to confirm:
```bash
aws s3 ls s3://.../data/hudi_cow_logical/.hoodie/ | tail -20
```

### Read returns 0 rows
Ensure the Hudi table path is correct and at least one write has completed:
```bash
aws s3 ls s3://.../data/hudi_cow_logical/.hoodie/
```

### Column `ts_millis_100` not found
The schema generated by `initial_batch.scala` places `ts_millis_*` columns at every
200th index (ts_millis_100, ts_millis_200, …) and `ts_micros_*` at odd-50th indexes.
Verify with:
```python
spark.read.format("hudi").load("<table_path>").printSchema()
```
Then update `MEASURE_COL` in `03_read_benchmark.py` to match an existing `ts_millis_*` column.
